                            <h2 class="title" id="overview_heading">Overview</h2>
                            <p>Nonprofit <a href="https://www.commonsense.org/20-years-of-impact/"><span>Common Sense Media</span></a> provides parents, educators, and policymakers with the information they need to make informed decisions about media and technology. <br><br>When the organization reached out to Free Range to create a digital and interactive report showcasing their 15 years of impact on the lives of children and families, we couldn’t wait to get started.</p>
                        
                        

                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_understand_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="1">Understand</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>Common Sense Media wanted to create a comprehensive overview of their work, research, and resources to celebrate their 15th anniversary. They also wanted to engage their stakeholders in a meaningful way.</p>
<p>To do this, they decided to create a digital and interactive impact report that would allow users to explore the information at their own pace.</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_explore_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading align-right" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="2">Explore</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>Utilizing insights and statistics collected by the CSM team from their own research, surveys, and prior reports, we envisioned a clean, intuitive user experience that would mix key pieces of copy with infographics, interactive charts, and videos.</p>
<p>We also prioritized accessibility, taking into account color contrast, font size, and other accessibility features to ensure all users could find the information they were looking for.&nbsp;</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_create_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="3">Create</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>The final report is designed to be visually appealing and user-friendly, giving users the opportunity to explore the data in a more engaging way than a traditional report would allow.</p>
                        


                        
                            <div class="mt-5">
                                <div id="hs_cos_wrapper_launch_heading" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_widget hs_cos_wrapper_type_module" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="widget" data-hs-cos-type="module"><!-- module html  -->










<h4 class="module custom-heading align-right" style="color: #FF4E00; border-color: #4A4A4A; border-width: 2px" data-number="4">Launch</h4>
</div>
                            </div>
                            <p>Following the success of the original 15th anniversary report, Common Sense Media reached out again earlier this year to create a similar interactive site for their <a href="https://www.commonsense.org/20-years-of-impact/"><span>20th anniversary</span></a>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>We were honored to help raise awareness of Common Sense Media's work.&nbsp;</p>
                        

                        
                        
